{
  "uid": "vb-trace-pipeline",
  "title": "Trace pipeline health",
  "description": "Whether the observability layer is telling the truth. Drops, back-pressure, partition maintenance and customer trace export. Audience: whoever is about to trust a trace or a timeline.",
  "tags": [
    "vectorbea",
    "telemetry",
    "traces"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "env",
        "label": "Environment",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "query": "label_values(job_last_success_timestamp_seconds, environment)",
        "refresh": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "current": {
          "text": "prod",
          "value": "prod"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Are we losing telemetry?",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Run events dropped",
      "description": "THE SERIOUS ONE. An event hole breaks timeline paging on ?afterSequence= and a lost RUN_FAILED is an outage reported as a success. The store applies back-pressure before it drops, so any drop means it blocked past AGENT_EVENT_BACKPRESSURE_TIMEOUT_MS — the database was not answering.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(worker_run_events_dropped_total{environment=~\"$env\"}[5m]) * 60)",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "dropped/min"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 20,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "red"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Spans dropped, by reason",
      "description": "A dropped span is a degraded trace — bad, but bounded. SpanWriter drops and counts by design rather than blocking execution. Also persisted to agent_runs.dropped_spans, because 'was this trace complete' gets asked hours later.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(worker_trace_spans_dropped_total{environment=~\"$env\"}[5m]) * 60)",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Customer OTLP exports dropped",
      "description": "A workspace's own observability endpoint is not accepting. This is a customer-visible failure of a feature they configured — check workspace_otel_exports.last_error.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(worker_trace_exports_dropped_total{environment=~\"$env\"}[5m]) * 60)",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "dropped/min"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Spans written",
      "description": "The denominator. A drop rate means nothing without it — 10 drops/min against 10,000 written is a different situation from 10 against 12.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(worker_trace_spans_written_total{environment=~\"$env\"}[5m]) * 60)",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "written/min"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Event-store back-pressure — DB pool wait",
      "description": "The upstream cause of nearly every event drop. Events block on the emitting thread waiting for a connection; when this climbs, drops follow.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 9
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, service) (rate(db_pool_wait_seconds_bucket{environment=~\"$env\"}[5m])))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "p95 {{service}}"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, service) (rate(db_pool_wait_seconds_bucket{environment=~\"$env\"}[5m])))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "p99 {{service}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Partitions and archive",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 17
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Partition drops refused by the gate",
      "description": "`work_outstanding` means the gate is correctly holding a drop because the export is behind. `gate_unavailable` is more urgent: the export state could not be read at all, so nothing will drop until a person acts.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(worker_partition_drops_gated_total{environment=~\"$env\"}[15m]) * 60)",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Partition maintenance passes",
      "description": "Whether the job that creates next month's partitions is actually running. run_events has NO default partition — when the last pre-created month elapses, every event write in the system errors.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 18
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(job_runs_total{environment=~\"$env\", job_name=\"partition-maintenance\"}[1h]) * 3600)",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}/h"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
